filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-11-08: the local IPC
ONLYOFFICE core 10.0 adds to kernel_network (Common/Network/network.pro,
WebSocket/src/localipc) is left out of the WebAssembly build.

It is a loopback request-response channel over asio sockets and
std::thread; nothing in core links against it but network.pro itself (read
at v10.0.0.169), x2t does not call it, and WebAssembly here has neither the
sockets nor the threads. Building it needs asio's headers from
socket.io-client-cpp, which core's tree does not carry (build_tools fetches
it for the desktop and server builds). Under CONFIG core_wasm, which
scripts/x2t/steps.sh sets, the block is skipped; every other build of core
is unchanged.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

diff --git a/Common/Network/network.pro b/Common/Network/network.pro
index f61846f1..7a56ab28 100644
--- a/Common/Network/network.pro
+++ b/Common/Network/network.pro
@@ -52,10 +52,13 @@ support_web_socket {
 }
 
 # LOCAL IPC (loopback request-response).
+# filex-office-editor: not in WebAssembly (no sockets, no threads; nothing in x2t calls it).
+!core_wasm {
 INCLUDEPATH += $$PWD/../3dParty/socketio/socket.io-client-cpp/lib/asio/asio/include
 HEADERS += $$PWD/WebSocket/include/localipc.h
 SOURCES += $$PWD/WebSocket/src/localipc/localipc.cpp
 core_linux:LIBS += -lpthread   # asio/std::thread (idempotent if websocket also added it)
+}
 
 # DOWNLOAD/UPLOAD
 include(./FileTransporter/filetransporter.pri)
